+# STORY-007 Phase 4 — Discovery Plan
+
+**Date:** 2026-04-29
+**Phase:** 4 (Analysis)
+**Story:** STORY-007 — Target API discovery in staging (schema + enum + rate-limit capture)
+**Model:** Sonnet (Phase 4 default)
+**Inputs:**
+- `features/story-007-target-staging-discovery/seed.md` — problem statement, OQ list, boundaries
+- `features/story-006-target-openapi-synthesis/target-openapi.yaml` — 24 operations, 25 schemas (baseline)
+- `features/story-001-target-amazon-field-gap/analysis.md` — 11 UNCLEAR rows, 23 OQs
+- `features/story-001-target-amazon-field-gap/selection.md` § 5–8 — staging-resolvable OQ triage
+
+> **Phase 4 deliverable for STORY-007** (from seed.md):
+> *"A discovery plan: list every endpoint, every probe (read/induced-error), expected output, and which OQ it resolves. Cite `target-openapi.yaml` operationId for each row."*
+
+---
+
+## 1. Executive Summary
+
+This discovery plan instruments all 24 Target Plus Partner API operations catalogued in `target-openapi.yaml` against `https://stage-api.target.com`. Of the 24 operations, **13 are GET (read-safe — execute immediately)**, **1 is a safe POST** (report creation, which only creates read artifacts — no listing or order impact), and **10 are write paths (PUT/POST) that must not be executed without operator approval**.
+
+Executing the 13 GET probes + 1 safe POST resolves **13 of 14 staging-resolvable open questions**. The remaining OQ (OQ-6, bulk product creation shape) requires a POST to `/products` or an Implementation PM enquiry; it is flagged as "operator approval required" and is out of scope for the automated harness run.
+
+Rate-limit measurement is embedded into each GET probe via a controlled burst sub-probe (10 rapid identical calls, measure latency + first 429 response). Error-envelope induction (OQ-13) is achieved by deliberately malforming GET requests (invalid seller_id, missing required params) — **no write endpoints are needed for OQ-13**.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Open-Question Register (staging-resolvable subset)
+
+The following OQs are scoped to this story. Each row shows the originating source, what staging data resolves it, and which probe delivers the answer.
+
+| OQ # | Question | Source | Resolved by probe(s) |
+|------|----------|--------|----------------------|
+| OQ-1 | `x-seller-token` expiry / refresh behavior | `analysis.md` Arch row 6; STORY-006 research | Any auth probe that waits ≥ token TTL, or observe 401 on any GET |
+| OQ-3 | Rate limits per endpoint (not documented anywhere) | `analysis.md` Arch row 3 | Burst sub-probes on every GET endpoint |
+| OQ-5 | `product_logitics` path typo — does the typo path return 200 or 404? | `target-openapi.yaml` `x-pdf-typo` annotation; STORY-002 p. 15 | `probe_product_logistics_typo` (GET both paths) |
+| OQ-6 | Bulk product creation endpoint shape (p. 11 — "Bulk Create New Product API") | STORY-002 research § 3 endpoint #9 note | `probe_bulk_product_endpoint_discovery` — **operator approval required before execution** |
+| OQ-7 | Full `GET /orders` response schema (4 UNCLEAR analysis.md rows ride on this) | `analysis.md` § 3.4 — item price/qty, buyer email, currency, address | `probe_released_orders` |
+| OQ-8 | Additional report types beyond `ALLOWED_ITEM_TYPES` | STORY-006 README OQ-8; `createReportRequest` description | `probe_create_report_request` (safe POST) |
+| OQ-9 | Return reason enum values (only undocumented) | `analysis.md` § 3.6; `ProductReturn` schema | `probe_product_returns` |
+| OQ-10 | Cancellation reason enum (only `ITEM_NOT_AVAILABLE` documented) | `analysis.md` § 3.4; `cancelOrderLine` description | `probe_order_cancellation_enum` — must coordinate with STORY-009 cert plan |
+| OQ-11 | Report status enum values (`COMPLETE`, `FAILED`? others?) | `ReportRequest.status` field — `x-confidence: unknown` | `probe_list_report_requests` + `probe_get_report_request` |
+| OQ-12 | Listing-error severity enum (only `CRITICAL` documented) | `analysis.md` § 3.1; `ListingError.error_severity` | `probe_listing_errors` |
+| OQ-13 | 4xx/5xx error response envelope (structure completely undocumented) | `analysis.md` Arch row 4; `target-openapi.yaml` — no 4xx responses defined | `probe_error_envelope_induction` (malformed GETs) |
+| OQ-19 | Payout filter parameters beyond `created_before` / `created_after` | `analysis.md` § 3.9; `getPayouts` parameters | `probe_payouts` |
+| OQ-20 | Product search / catalog browse capability (GET /products?) | `analysis.md` § 3.1; no `GET /products` in `target-openapi.yaml` | `probe_catalog_browse_discovery` (undocumented path probe) |
+| Pricing currency | USD assumed but not stated on `Price` object | `analysis.md` § 3.3 UNCLEAR row | `probe_released_orders` (look for `currency` field in order response) |
+
+**Total staging-resolvable:** 14 items (13 automated + 1 requiring operator approval).
+
+**OQs NOT resolved by this story** (per seed.md § "Open questions NOT resolved"): OQ-2, OQ-4, OQ-14, OQ-15, OQ-16, OQ-17, OQ-18, OQ-21, OQ-22, OQ-23.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Endpoint Inventory and Probe Plan
+
+### 3.1 GET (read-safe) probes — execute in harness without operator approval
+
+All probes call `https://stage-api.target.com`. Auth headers: `x-api-key`, `x-seller-id`, `x-seller-token` injected via DI; never logged or committed.
+
+Each GET probe also includes a **burst sub-probe** (10 rapid identical GETs with 50 ms inter-call delay) to measure rate limits. Capture: first 429 or throttling signal, latency distribution P50/P95.
+
+---
+
+#### Probe 1 — `probe_taxonomy` → `getTaxonomy`
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| `operationId` | `getTaxonomy` |
+| Path | `GET /item_taxonomies/v2/taxonomy` |
+| Params | `type=ITEM_TYPE&target=EXTERNAL` |
+| OQs resolved | None directly (taxonomy schema already largely inferred); confirms `TaxonomyResponse` wire shape |
+| Expected output | Taxonomy tree with item-type nodes; pagination fields if response is large |
+| Capture file | `captures/taxonomy.json` |
+| Schema delta check | Confirm `TaxonomyResponse` fields; promote `x-confidence: inferred` → `verified` if shape matches |
+| Rate-limit probe | Yes (burst sub-probe) |
+| Credential redaction | `x-api-key`, `x-seller-id`, `x-seller-token` values replaced with `[REDACTED]` |
+| Write risk | None — read only |
+
+---
+
+#### Probe 2 — `probe_taxonomy_assignments` → `getTaxonomyAssignments`
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| `operationId` | `getTaxonomyAssignments` |
+| Path | `GET /item_taxonomies/v2/assignments` |
+| Params | `taxonomy_id=<first node from probe_taxonomy>&attribute_group=SELLING,CORE,TAX,LOGISTICS&target=EXTERNAL` |
+| OQs resolved | None directly; confirms `AttributeAssignmentResponse` structure; pagination behavior (page size 250) |
+| Expected output | Attribute groups and attribute list for a taxonomy node |
+| Capture file | `captures/taxonomy_assignments.json` |
+| Schema delta check | Confirm attribute group structure; any undocumented fields |
+| Rate-limit probe | Yes |
+| Write risk | None |
+
+---
+
+#### Probe 3 — `probe_taxonomy_attribute_values` → `getTaxonomyAttributeValues`
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| `operationId` | `getTaxonomyAttributeValues` |
+| Path | `GET /item_taxonomies/v2/attribute_values` |
+| Params | `taxonomy_id=<first node>&attribute_id=<first attribute from probe_taxonomy_assignments>&target=EXTERNAL` |
+| OQs resolved | None directly; confirms `AttributeValuesResponse` shape; page size 100 behavior |
+| Expected output | List of allowed enum values for one attribute |
+| Capture file | `captures/taxonomy_attribute_values.json` |
+| Schema delta check | Confirm value list structure; any undocumented `confidence` or `deprecated` flags |
+| Rate-limit probe | Yes |
+| Write risk | None |
+
+---
+
+#### Probe 4 — `probe_list_report_requests` → `listReportRequests`
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| `operationId` | `listReportRequests` |
+| Path | `GET /sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/report_requests` |
+| Params | `seller_id` from credentials |
+| OQs resolved | **OQ-11** (report status enum — observe `status` values in any existing requests); **OQ-8** (any non-`ALLOWED_ITEM_TYPES` report types in existing requests) |
+| Expected output | Array of `ReportRequest` objects; each has `status`, `report_type`, `request_id`, `created_at`, `download_url` (if complete) |
+| Capture file | `captures/report_requests_list.json` |
+| Schema delta check | Record all unique `status` values observed → update `ReportRequest.status` enum in `target-openapi.yaml`; record all `report_type` values |
+| Rate-limit probe | Yes |
+| Write risk | None |
+
+---
+
+#### Probe 5 — `probe_get_report_request` → `getReportRequest`
+
+| Field | Value |
+|-------|-------|
+| `operationId` | `getReportRequest` |
+| Path | `GET /sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/report_requests/{report_request_id}` |
+| Params | Use `report_request_id` from most recent complete request in probe_list_report_requests |
+| OQs resolved | **OQ-11** (confirm complete status enum value; observe `download_url` presence/absence); **OQ-8** (report type label in individual record) |
+| Expected output | Single `ReportRequest` with `download_url` when `status=COMPLETE` |
