+## 5. Rate-Limit Measurement Methodology
+
+Each GET probe includes a burst sub-probe immediately after the primary call succeeds:
+
+1. **Burst sequence:** 10 calls to the same endpoint with identical params, 50 ms inter-call sleep
+2. **Measurements recorded:** Per-call latency (ms), HTTP status of each call, `Retry-After` or `X-RateLimit-*` headers if present, timestamp of first 429 (if any)
+3. **Calculation:** Estimated requests-per-second ceiling = (number of calls before first 429) / (elapsed time in seconds)
+4. **If no 429 in 10 calls:** increase burst to 50 calls with 10 ms inter-call sleep. If still no throttle: report "rate limit not measurable in staging at N req/s burst"
+5. **Capture file:** `captures/rate_limits.json` — one entry per endpoint with burst results
+
+**Why this matters:** STORY-013 (Pricing) and STORY-014 (Inventory) cannot size their per-item loop queues without empirical rate limits. The measured ceiling sets the floor for queue batch-size and retry backoff design in Phase 6.
