+## 7. Confidence Thresholds for Spec Patches
+
+After the harness run, `target-openapi.yaml` patches promote field confidence as follows:
+
+| Observed condition | Confidence change |
+|-------------------|-------------------|
+| Field observed in wire response with exact name match | `unknown` → `verified` |
+| Field observed but with different name than spec | `inferred` → `verified` (with note: "actual name differs from PDF") |
+| Enum observed with additional values beyond spec | Note all new values; mark enum `x-confidence: verified` |
+| Field in spec but NOT observed in any response | `inferred` → remains `inferred` (add `x-staging-note: not observed`) |
+| New field in wire response NOT in spec | Add to schema as `x-confidence: verified` with `x-source-page: "staging-discovery-2026-04-29"` |
