+# STORY-007 Phase 6 — Feature Spec: Target Staging Discovery Harness
+
+**Date:** 2026-04-29
+**Phase:** 6 (Design — Lite/Medium)
+**Story:** STORY-007 — Target API discovery in staging (schema + enum + rate-limit capture)
+**Model:** Opus (tier-1)
+**Scope:** Medium
+**Inputs:**
+- `features/story-007-target-staging-discovery/seed.md`
+- `features/story-007-target-staging-discovery/analysis.md` (Phase 4 — 20 probes, 14 OQs)
+- `features/story-006-target-openapi-synthesis/target-openapi.yaml` (24 operations, baseline)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Overview
+
+A one-shot Python CLI tool (`tools/target-discovery/`) that authenticates against `https://stage-api.target.com`, executes 20 probes across all 24 Target Plus Partner API operations, captures raw responses (credential-redacted), measures rate limits, and writes:
+
+1. `features/story-007-target-staging-discovery/discovery-report.md` — OQ resolution table, observed schemas, enum values, rate-limit measurements, error envelope shapes
+2. Patches to `target-openapi.yaml` — promote `x-confidence: unknown` fields to `verified`
+3. Patches to `analysis.md` — resolve UNCLEAR rows
+
+This is **NOT** a production service. No FastAPI, no Postgres, no Docker. It's a developer tool run once during Week 1 of the 30-day staging certification window.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Module Structure
+
+```
+tools/
+  target-discovery/
+    __init__.py          # Package marker; exports version string
+    cli.py               # Click CLI entry point; orchestrates probe execution
+    client.py            # TargetDiscoveryClient — DI'd httpx.Client wrapper
+    probes.py            # One probe_* function per endpoint (20 probes)
+    redact.py            # Credential + PII redaction before disk write
+    rate_limit.py        # Burst sub-probe runner + measurement recorder
+    captures/
+      .gitkeep           # Placeholder; captures/*.json written at runtime
+tests/
+  discovery/
+    __init__.py
+    conftest.py          # Shared fixtures: mock client, respx routes, tmp captures dir
+    test_no_production_calls.py
+    test_staging_only_baseurl.py
+    test_credentials_redacted_in_logs.py
+    test_oq_resolution.py
+    test_spec_patches.py
+```
+
+**Why this structure:**
+- `tools/` (not `app/`) — signals this is a one-shot developer tool, not production code
+- One module per concern — `client.py` owns HTTP, `redact.py` owns scrubbing, `probes.py` owns endpoint logic
+- `captures/` checked into git (with `.gitkeep`) so the output path exists; actual `.json` files are `.gitignore`'d to prevent accidental credential commits
+
+---
+
+## 3. Component Design
+
+### 3.1 `client.py` — `TargetDiscoveryClient`
+
+```python
+@dataclass
+class TargetDiscoveryClient:
+    """DI'd HTTP client for Target staging API. Never instantiated with production URL."""
+
+    base_url: str = "https://stage-api.target.com"
+    api_key: str = ""        # from env TARGET_API_KEY
+    seller_id: str = ""      # from env TARGET_SELLER_ID
+    seller_token: str = ""   # from env TARGET_SELLER_TOKEN
+
+    def get(self, path: str, params: dict | None = None, timeout: float = 30.0) -> httpx.Response:
+        """Execute GET against staging. Returns raw httpx.Response."""
+
+    def post(self, path: str, json: dict | None = None, timeout: float = 30.0) -> httpx.Response:
+        """Execute POST against staging. Only used for safe report creation."""
+
+    def _headers(self) -> dict[str, str]:
+        """Build auth headers. Never log the return value."""
+```
+
+**Design decisions:**
+
+| Decision | Rationale |
+|----------|-----------|
+| `httpx.Client` (sync), not `httpx.AsyncClient` | One-shot CLI; no concurrency benefit. Simpler to debug, test, and trace. |
+| `base_url` defaults to staging | Defense-in-depth: even if env is misconfigured, default is safe. Tests assert this. |
+| Credentials from env vars only | Never hardcoded, never in CLI args (visible in `ps`), never in config files committed to git. |
+| `@dataclass` not class hierarchy | Single implementation — no abstract base, no interface. Rule of Three not met. |
+| No retry logic in client | Probes handle their own retry/skip. Client is a thin HTTP wrapper. Retries are probe-level policy. |
+
+**Credential loading:**
+
+```python
+@classmethod
+def from_env(cls) -> "TargetDiscoveryClient":
+    """Load credentials from environment. Raises ValueError if any are missing."""
+    api_key = os.environ.get("TARGET_API_KEY", "")
+    seller_id = os.environ.get("TARGET_SELLER_ID", "")
+    seller_token = os.environ.get("TARGET_SELLER_TOKEN", "")
+    if not all([api_key, seller_id, seller_token]):
+        raise ValueError(
+            "Missing TARGET_API_KEY, TARGET_SELLER_ID, or TARGET_SELLER_TOKEN. "
+            "Set all three environment variables before running discovery."
+        )
+    return cls(api_key=api_key, seller_id=seller_id, seller_token=seller_token)
+```
+
+**Failure mode:**
+
+| Dependency | Unavailable Behavior | Rationale |
+|------------|---------------------|-----------|
+| `stage-api.target.com` | Fail-closed: log error, skip probe, record "UNREACHABLE" in report | Cannot substitute staging data; a failed probe is an honest "unknown" |
+| Env credentials missing | Fail-closed: raise `ValueError` at startup, abort entire run | No point running any probes without auth |
+| Single endpoint 5xx | Fail-closed for that probe: capture error response, continue to next probe | One bad endpoint shouldn't abort the entire run |
+| Token expired (401) | Fail-closed: log "re-auth required", abort remaining probes | Retrying with a dead token is pointless; operator must rotate |
+
+### 3.2 `redact.py` — Credential and PII Scrubbing
+
+```python
+CREDENTIAL_KEYS = ["x-api-key", "x-seller-id", "x-seller-token", "tgtrt"]
+CREDENTIAL_PLACEHOLDER = {
+    "x-api-key": "[REDACTED-API-KEY]",
+    "x-seller-id": "[REDACTED-SELLER-ID]",
+    "x-seller-token": "[REDACTED-SELLER-TOKEN]",
+    "tgtrt": "[REDACTED-TGTRT]",
+}
+
+PII_KEYS = ["name", "first_name", "last_name", "email", "phone",
+            "address_line_1", "address_line_2", "address_line_3",
+            "zip_code", "postal_code"]
+PII_PLACEHOLDER = "[REDACTED-PII]"
+
+def redact_response(response_dict: dict, credential_values: list[str]) -> dict:
+    """Deep-copy response, replace credential values and PII fields.
+
+    Args:
+        response_dict: Parsed JSON response body.
+        credential_values: Actual credential strings to scrub from ANY value
+                          (catches credentials leaked in error messages, etc.)
+
+    Returns:
+        Redacted copy. Original is never modified.
+    """
+
+def redact_headers(headers: dict, credential_values: list[str]) -> dict:
+    """Redact auth header values in captured request/response headers."""
+```
+
+**Design decisions:**
+
+| Decision | Rationale |
+|----------|-----------|
+| Deep-copy before redaction | Original `httpx.Response` stays in memory for probe logic; disk never sees raw values |
+| Scrub by value (not just key) | Credentials can appear in error messages, URLs, or unexpected fields. Value-scan catches all. |
+| PII redaction by key name | Order address fields follow predictable naming; key-based is sufficient |
+| No regex for credential detection | Credential values are known at runtime (loaded from env). Exact-match is more reliable than pattern-guessing. |
+
+### 3.3 `rate_limit.py` — Burst Measurement
+
+```python
+@dataclass
+class BurstResult:
+    endpoint: str
+    total_calls: int
+    first_429_at: int | None        # Call number (1-indexed) that got 429, or None
+    latency_p50_ms: float
+    latency_p95_ms: float
+    retry_after_header: str | None  # Value of Retry-After if present
+    rate_limit_headers: dict        # Any X-RateLimit-* headers observed
+
+def run_burst(
+    client: TargetDiscoveryClient,
+    path: str,
+    params: dict | None = None,
+    burst_size: int = 10,
+    inter_call_ms: int = 50,
+) -> BurstResult:
+    """Fire `burst_size` identical GETs with `inter_call_ms` sleep between calls.
+
+    If no 429 in initial burst: escalate to 50 calls with 10ms delay.
+    Capture latency distribution and any throttling signals.
+    """
+```
+
+**Measurement protocol** (from analysis.md § 5):
+1. First pass: 10 calls, 50 ms inter-call delay
+2. If no 429: second pass with 50 calls, 10 ms inter-call delay
+3. If still no 429: record "rate limit not measurable in staging at N req/s burst"
+4. Capture per-endpoint: P50/P95 latency, first 429 position, `Retry-After` value, `X-RateLimit-*` headers
+
+### 3.4 `probes.py` — Probe Functions
+
+Each probe follows a consistent signature:
+
+```python
+@dataclass
+class ProbeResult:
+    probe_name: str
+    operation_id: str
+    http_status: int
+    response_body: dict           # Already redacted
+    request_headers: dict         # Already redacted
+    response_headers: dict
+    oqs_resolved: list[str]       # e.g., ["OQ-7", "OQ-Pricing-Currency"]
+    schema_deltas: list[str]      # Human-readable notes for spec patching
+    burst_result: BurstResult | None
+    error: str | None             # If probe failed, why
+
+def probe_taxonomy(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_taxonomy_assignments(client: TargetDiscoveryClient, taxonomy_id: str) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_taxonomy_attribute_values(client: TargetDiscoveryClient, taxonomy_id: str, attribute_id: str) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_list_report_requests(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_get_report_request(client: TargetDiscoveryClient, request_id: str) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_distribution_centers(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_shipping_methods(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_product_status(client: TargetDiscoveryClient, product_id: str) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_released_orders(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_order_address(client: TargetDiscoveryClient, order_id: str) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_product_returns(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_payouts(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_listing_errors(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_create_report_request(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_bulk_product_endpoint_discovery(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_cancellation_reason_enum(client: TargetDiscoveryClient, order_line_id: str) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_product_logistics_typo(client: TargetDiscoveryClient, product_id: str) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_catalog_browse_discovery(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_error_envelope_induction(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+def probe_token_expiry(client: TargetDiscoveryClient) -> ProbeResult: ...
+```
+
+**Probe execution rules:**
+- Each probe catches `httpx.HTTPError` and returns a `ProbeResult` with `error` set — never raises
+- Probes that depend on prior data (e.g., `probe_order_address` needs `order_id` from `probe_released_orders`) receive the dependency as a parameter; the CLI orchestrates the data flow
+- Probes marked "operator approval required" (15, 16) check for `--approved-writes` flag; if absent, return `ProbeResult(error="SKIPPED — requires operator approval")`
+- Every probe that runs a burst sub-probe populates `burst_result`
+
+### 3.5 `cli.py` — Orchestrator
+
+```python
+@click.group()
+def cli():
+    """Target API staging discovery harness."""
+
+@cli.command()
+@click.option("--approved-writes", is_flag=True, default=False,
+              help="Enable operator-approved write probes (OQ-6, OQ-10). Default: disabled.")
+@click.option("--captures-dir", type=click.Path(), default="tools/target-discovery/captures",
+              help="Directory for captured responses.")
+@click.option("--report-path", type=click.Path(),
+              default="features/story-007-target-staging-discovery/discovery-report.md",
+              help="Path to write discovery report.")
+def capture_all(approved_writes: bool, captures_dir: str, report_path: str):
+    """Run all probes in execution sequence (Phases A–J from analysis.md)."""
+```
+
+**Execution sequence** (from analysis.md § 9):
+
+```
+Phase A: Auth validation
+  → probe_shipping_methods (validates credentials)
+  → If 401/403: abort with "credentials invalid" message
+
+Phase B: Reference data (no dependencies)
+  → probe_taxonomy
+  → probe_taxonomy_assignments (uses taxonomy_id from Phase B.1)
+  → probe_taxonomy_attribute_values (uses taxonomy_id + attribute_id from Phase B.2)
+  → probe_distribution_centers
+
+Phase C: Reports (async — start early, poll later)
+  → probe_create_report_request (safe POST)
+  → probe_list_report_requests
+
+Phase D: Product / listing state
+  → probe_product_status (if staging products exist; else skip with note)
+  → probe_catalog_browse_discovery
+  → probe_product_logistics_typo (if product_id available; else skip)
+
+Phase E: Orders and fulfillment
+  → probe_released_orders
+  → probe_order_address (uses order_id from Phase E.1; skip if no orders)
+
+Phase F: Reporting endpoints
+  → probe_product_returns
+  → probe_payouts
+  → probe_listing_errors
+
+Phase G: Error envelope induction
+  → probe_error_envelope_induction (malformed GETs against known-good endpoints)
+
+Phase H: Auth / token
+  → probe_token_expiry
+
+Phase I: Async report resolution
+  → probe_get_report_request (poll until terminal status or 60s timeout)
+
+Phase J: Operator-approved writes (if --approved-writes)
+  → probe_bulk_product_endpoint_discovery
+  → probe_cancellation_reason_enum (or defer to STORY-009)
+```
+
+**CLI output contract:**
+
+```
+[discovery] Loaded credentials from environment
+[discovery] Phase A: Validating auth via getShippingMethods...
+[discovery] Phase A: OK (200) — 12 shipping methods
+[discovery] Phase B: Reference data (4 probes)...
+  ...
+[discovery] Captures written to tools/target-discovery/captures/
+[discovery] discovery-report.md written to features/story-007-target-staging-discovery/
+[discovery] Summary: 18/20 probes succeeded, 2 skipped (operator approval required)
+[discovery] OQ resolution: 11 resolved, 2 still unknown, 1 deferred
