+
+## 4. Error Handling Design
+
+### 4.1 Error Response Format
+
+This is a CLI tool, not an API server — no RFC 7807 applies. Errors are structured in `ProbeResult.error` strings and in the `discovery-report.md` output.
+
+### 4.2 Error Categories
+
+| Error | Handling | Log output |
+|-------|----------|------------|
+| Missing env credentials | `ValueError` at startup; abort entire run | `[discovery] FATAL: Missing TARGET_API_KEY...` |
+| 401 Unauthorized | Abort remaining probes; record all completed results | `[discovery] FATAL: 401 on {endpoint} — token expired or invalid. Re-auth required.` |
+| 403 Forbidden | Record probe as failed; continue | `[discovery] WARN: 403 on {operation_id} — insufficient permissions` |
+| 404 Not Found | Expected for path-discovery probes (OQ-5, OQ-20); record as valid signal | `[discovery] INFO: 404 on {path} — endpoint does not exist` |
+| 429 Too Many Requests | Expected during burst probes; record as rate-limit data point | `[discovery] INFO: 429 on {operation_id} at call #{n} — rate limit found` |
+| 5xx Server Error | Capture request+response; skip probe; do NOT retry | `[discovery] ERROR: {status} on {operation_id} — server error. Captured for escalation.` |
+| `httpx.ConnectError` | Staging unreachable; abort all probes | `[discovery] FATAL: Cannot reach stage-api.target.com` |
+| `httpx.TimeoutException` | Record probe as timed out; continue | `[discovery] WARN: Timeout on {operation_id} after {timeout}s` |
+
+### 4.3 What Is NOT Logged
+
+- Credential values (`x-api-key`, `x-seller-id`, `x-seller-token`, `tgtrt`)
+- PII from order addresses
+- Full request/response bodies (those go to redacted capture files only)
+
