+
+## 5. Dependency Injection Pattern
+
+```python
+# In tests:
+from tools.target_discovery.client import TargetDiscoveryClient
+
+def make_mock_client(base_url="https://stage-api.target.com") -> TargetDiscoveryClient:
+    return TargetDiscoveryClient(
+        base_url=base_url,
+        api_key="test-key",
+        seller_id="test-seller",
+        seller_token="test-token",
+    )
+
+# In conftest.py — respx mocks all outbound HTTP:
+@pytest.fixture
+def mock_client(respx_mock):
+    client = make_mock_client()
+    respx_mock.get(re.compile(r"https://stage-api\.target\.com/.*")).respond(200, json={})
+    return client
+```
+
+**DI enforcement:** `TargetDiscoveryClient` is the ONLY module that calls `httpx`. All probes receive it as a parameter. Tests inject a mock. Phase 7 test `test_no_production_calls.py` uses `respx` to assert zero calls to `api.target.com`.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Shared Utilities (Epic Cross-Story Checklist)
+
+STORY-007 is the gating story for STORY-008..017. While the discovery harness itself is one-shot, the following patterns from this story will be reused:
+
+| Utility | File | Owner Story | Consumers | Reuse Scope |
+|---------|------|-------------|-----------|-------------|
+| `redact.py` credential scrubbing | `tools/target-discovery/redact.py` | STORY-007 | STORY-008..017 (test fixtures) | Pattern only — downstream stories will have their own `app/core/redact.py` based on the same credential list. STORY-007 establishes the canonical credential key list. |
+| Auth header construction | `tools/target-discovery/client.py` | STORY-007 | STORY-008 (will build production `TargetClient`) | Pattern only — STORY-008 designs its own `app/clients/target.py` informed by STORY-007's observations (token TTL, header format). |
+| Error envelope schema | `discovery-report.md` § OQ-13 | STORY-007 | ALL downstream stories | Data — STORY-007 captures the error shape; all stories implement error handling against it. |
+
+**Decision:** No shared importable module is created across stories. STORY-007 lives in `tools/` (one-shot); STORY-008+ lives in `app/` (production). The reuse is knowledge transfer (captured schemas, observed enums), not code sharing. This avoids coupling a throwaway discovery tool to production architecture.
