+## 16. Key Design Decisions
+
+| Decision | Choice | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|-----------|
+| Sync httpx, not async | `httpx.Client` (sync) | One-shot CLI; no concurrency needed; simpler debugging |
+| Click for CLI | `click` over `argparse` | Better testing support (`CliRunner`); cleaner option syntax |
+| No database | No Postgres, no SQLite | One-shot capture to files; no persistence beyond the report |
+| No production code path | `tools/` not `app/` | Discovery harness is throwaway; production client designed in STORY-008 |
+| Captures as JSON + report as Markdown | JSON for machine-readable; MD for human-readable | Downstream stories parse JSON captures; humans read the report |
+| No retry in client | Probe-level skip/abort | Retrying blindly against staging risks masking intermittent issues; explicit per-probe policy is safer |
+| Probe functions return `ProbeResult`, never raise | Uniform error handling | CLI can always write a complete report regardless of individual probe failures |
