+### 2.1 `test_no_production_calls.py` — Gate 2a External API Isolation
+
+**Purpose:** Assert that no probe function ever makes an outbound HTTP call to `https://api.target.com` (production). All traffic must route to `https://stage-api.target.com`.
+
+**Technique:** `respx.mock` intercepts all outbound httpx calls. A production route is registered; after invoking `probe_shipping_methods()`, we assert the production route was never matched.
+
+**Acceptance criteria:**
+- `production_route.called` is `False` after running any probe
+- `result.http_status == 200` (probe succeeded against staging)
+- `result.error is None` (probe completed cleanly)
+
+**RED → GREEN transition:**
+- Implement `probe_shipping_methods()` to call `client.get("/shipping_methods")` and populate a real `ProbeResult` from the response. Implement `client.get()` to use `httpx.Client` internally, enabling `respx` interception. When the stub is replaced, both `http_status` and `error` assertions pass, and the production route remains uncalled.
+
+**Tests in this file:**
+- `test_no_call_to_production_url` — primary gate assertion
+- `test_probe_result_has_no_production_url_in_body` — secondary: production URL must not leak into captured body
